+# R9 Swift completion bridge derivation
+
+This bridge is a narrow, single-window derivation of the fixed
+`screencapturekit 8.0.1` Swift package. It replaces this crate's dependency on
+the general SCK wrapper and its AppleMetal/streaming graph. It is not a
+drop-in replacement for that package and does not relicense it.
+
+## Fixed registry input
+
+- Crate: `screencapturekit 8.0.1`
+- Registry archive: `screencapturekit-8.0.1.crate`
+  - bytes: `216361`
+  - SHA-256: `9ddaa8d6b16a2762c9a97c9a6297f04cb8ded0487e5ef02dc98b4e2bee3a26c7`
+- `.cargo_vcs_info.json` git revision:
+  `2a9f13bcbeadb0aabc5596f0ff3d2ba71da8c1d0`
+- Upstream package source root: `swift-bridge/Sources/ScreenCaptureKitBridge/`
+- Registry/source tree is read-only for this round. The archive files are not
+  copied into the candidate; only the hashes and the derived Swift file are.
+
+## Source files read for the derivation
+
+All paths are relative to the extracted `screencapturekit-8.0.1` package.
+
+| File | SHA-256 | Used for |
+|---|---|---|
+| `swift-bridge/Sources/ScreenCaptureKitBridge/ScreenshotManager.swift` | `6737a988e36c183c7108d906aaf8dfd163d943355bf1d22318be4bc4448d5238` | `SCScreenshotManager.captureImage` completion form and CGImage result |
+| `swift-bridge/Sources/ScreenCaptureKitBridge/ShareableContent.swift` | `8b157597be5098d7024a902c8d4fffcc1ef78689eb0638b0c264c1bbbb2b6c43` | `SCShareableContent.getExcludingDesktopWindows` and window identity fields |
+| `swift-bridge/Sources/ScreenCaptureKitBridge/StreamConfiguration.swift` | `f35fe19942db95cf100c07c71a30f74b7d8aee1d598f33d91bffb422d913c1be` | `SCStreamConfiguration` width/height/showsCursor/pixelFormat |
+| `swift-bridge/Sources/ScreenCaptureKitBridge/Core.swift` | `c8f3959d4df06d5ab710ade3bbdacccccfdc41af131aea89caacba96ec8a7e27` | Window/filter bridge concepts and retained-pointer handling to remove |
+| `swift-bridge/Sources/ScreenCaptureKitBridge/CoreGraphicsStrided.swift` | `b86b0a4250b363ce59d29686e952aafa208ae604b79e89dd0d9c2da175b50b45` | CMYK/bounded pixel extent and CGImage-to-RGBA conversion rules |
+
+The general wrapper's `Stream.swift`, `RecordingOutput.swift`,
+`ContentSharingPicker.swift`, `AudioDevices.swift`, `Metal/Metal.swift` and
+`CoreMedia/CoreMedia.swift` are deliberately not read into the candidate graph.
+The target crate compiles none of them.
+
+## Derived delta
+
+Kept semantics:
+
+- On-screen, non-desktop window enumeration through
+  `SCShareableContent.getExcludingDesktopWindows(false, onScreenWindowsOnly: true)`.
+- Exact `windowID` match, then `owningApplication.processID`, `windowLayer` and
+  `frame` as the selected identity.
+- `SCContentFilter(desktopIndependentWindow:)` for the one selected window.
+- `filter.pointPixelScale` and `filter.contentRect` for output sizing.
+- `SCStreamConfiguration` with `showsCursor = false`.
+- `SCScreenshotManager.captureImage(contentFilter:configuration:)` completion
+  callback and a bounded `CGImage` to RGBA conversion.
+
+Removed from the derived graph:
+
+- The Rust `screencapturekit` wrapper crate, `apple-metal` and `apple-cf`
+  dependencies used by the R8 capture root.
+- `SCStream`, recording outputs, audio devices, content-sharing picker, Metal
+  texture bridging and all stream lifecycle code.
+- Swift `Task`/`async` wrappers, opaque C userdata pointers and retained
+  CF/SCK pointer handoff. The R9 bridge passes scalar callbacks directly.
+- Two-second plan cache, timeouts, retries, shell/SkyLight fallback and consent
+  helpers remain absent, as in R8.
+
+Changed for this round:
+
+- The release callback is an explicit
+  `@convention(c) (UInt64) -> Void` parameter, matching the C ABI instead of
+  relying on an `@_silgen_name` symbol and Swift calling convention.
+- `LifecycleGate` makes enumeration, admission, capture and terminal delivery
+  once-only, so a duplicate framework callback cannot enter admission or
+  terminalize an operation whose first capture is still in flight.
+- `outputWidth * outputHeight * 4` is checked with
+  `multipliedReportingOverflow` before `SCScreenshotManager.captureImage`, and is
+  rejected against both the pixel budget and `maxRGBABytes` before any capture
+  starts.
+- `contentRect` is usable only when both width and height are finite and
+  positive; otherwise both axes fall back to the enumerated frame. This keeps
+  the R8 two-axis semantics instead of mixing one content axis with one frame
+  axis.
+- `configuration.pixelFormat` is explicitly
+  `kCVPixelFormatType_32BGRA`, so a framework default change cannot silently
+  alter the surface format.
+- The bridge owns one `RGBABuffer`. `completion` borrows it for the C callback
+  only; the buffer is deallocated and then `payloadReleased(requestID)` is sent.
+  Capacity is released only on that notification.
+
+Pixel semantics note: `renderRGBA` uses
+`CGImageAlphaInfo.premultipliedLast` with device RGB, matching the R8
+`CGImage` conversion. The PNG encoder writes these bytes as-is; transparency is
+not un-premultiplied. This document records the encoding equivalence; it does
+not claim a colour-management conversion beyond the R8 path.
+
+## Lifecycle limits (not closed by this round)
+
+- `payload_released` means the bridge-owned pixel storage and its C callback
+  borrow have been handed back. It is not evidence that the OS/ScreenCaptureKit
+  callback thread has returned, and it is not a native `Fenced` or `Drained`
+  result.
+- Cancelling an observation closes result reception only. A capture already
+  admitted in Swift may still start; the late result is dropped. Cancellation
+  before admission never starts a screenshot.
+- A native completion that never calls back keeps its bounded slot and the
+  observer waiting. There is deliberately no timeout that frees it.
+
+## Build and ABI evidence
+
+- Compiler: `/Library/Developer/CommandLineTools/usr/bin/swiftc`,
+  `Apple Swift version 6.4 (swiftlang-6.4.0.34.1 clang-2100.3.34.1)`.
+- SDK selector: `macosx27.0`, path
+  `/Library/Developer/CommandLineTools/SDKs/MacOSX.sdk`, reported version `27.0`.
+- Swift compile flags: `-parse-as-library -emit-object -swift-version 5 -O
+  -target arm64-apple-macos14.2 -sdk <SDK>`.
+- Object `LC_BUILD_VERSION`: `platform 1`, `minos 14.2`, `sdk 27.0`.
+- Real autolink entries include `-framework ScreenCaptureKit`,
+  `-framework Foundation`, `-framework CoreFoundation`, `-framework Metal`,
+  `-lswiftCore`, `-lswift_Concurrency`, `-lswiftMetal`, `-lswiftAVFoundation`,
+  `-lswiftCoreAudio`, `-lswiftCoreImage`, `-lswiftCoreMIDI`, `-lswiftIOKit`,
+  `-lswiftQuartzCore`, `-lswiftSpatial`, `-lswiftUniformTypeIdentifiers`,
+  `-lswiftXPC`, `-lswiftos` and `-lswiftsimd`.
+- The object defines `__swift_FORCE_LOAD_$_swiftMetal` and the other overlay
+  force-load symbols, but no `libswiftCompatibility56` or
+  `libswiftCompatibilityPacks` force-load. Those compat archives are therefore
+  not a build prerequisite; the build resolves the real autolink stubs from
+  `<SDK>/usr/lib/swift`.
+- The retained `-framework Metal`, `-lswiftMetal` and
+  `__swift_FORCE_LOAD_$_swiftMetal` entries are system framework/Swift-overlay
+  autolinks required by the SDK modules. They are not the removed `apple-metal`
+  crate, the upstream `swift-bridge/Sources/Metal/Metal.swift` texture wrapper,
+  or any recording/stream graph compiled by this candidate. System
+  ScreenCaptureKit may still use Metal internally; this round makes no claim
+  that it does not.
+- The independent consumer is linked with the same `-Wl,-syslibroot,<SDK>` and
+  records `minos 14.2`, `sdk 27.0`, `LC_RPATH=/usr/lib/swift`.
+
+An earlier local attempt pinned `macosx15.2` after a non-reproducible compiler
+diagnostic. Controller-run and repeated local builds then compiled the full
+bridge with SDK `27.0` with exit 0 and empty stderr. This document therefore
+does not claim that SDK 27 is incompatible with Swift 6.4; the 15.2 pin was a
+misdiagnosis and is not used.
+
+## License
+
+`screencapturekit 8.0.1` is dual-licensed. The original texts are retained
+verbatim next to this file:
+
+- `native/licenses/LICENSE-MIT`
+  - bytes: `1091`
+  - SHA-256: `5464a5ed6a2143a9d31e5516c7336a312c3c067cdc6ad15323f18fdf8d9755ae`
+- `native/licenses/LICENSE-APACHE`
+  - bytes: `11358`
+  - SHA-256: `cfc7749b96f63bd31c3c42b5c471bf756814053e847c10f3eb003417bc523d30`
+
+The CUA root `MIT` text (`crates/cua-macos-visual/LICENSE-MIT`) does not cover
+the derived ScreenCaptureKit material. This archive records the source and
+license relationship; it is not a legal adoption decision.
